.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-gist-push 1  "snip 0.5.5" 
.SH NAME
snip\-gist\-push \- Create the snippet\*(Aqs gist, or update it when one already exists
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip gist push\fR [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-public\fR] [\fB\-\-desc\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-new\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-simplified\-ui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-readme\fR] [\fB\-w\fR|\fB\-\-web\fR] [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create the snippet\*(Aqs gist, or update it when one already exists
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-public\fR
List the gist publicly. Only applies when creating; gist visibility cannot be changed afterwards
.TP
\fB\-\-desc\fR \fI<DESC>\fR
Gist description. Defaults to the snippet title, then to the description recorded by the previous push
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-new\fR
Publish a new gist and replace the recorded one, leaving the old gist on GitHub
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-notes\fR
Publish fragment notes as separate Markdown files
.TP
\fB\-\-simplified\-ui\fR[=\fI<BOOL>\fR]
Use square TUI bars without Powerline font glyphs for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
true
.IP \(bu 2
false
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-readme\fR
Leave the snippet README out of the gist
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-web\fR
Open the gist in a browser afterwards
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR \fI<IF_HASH>\fR
Refuse the push unless the snippet still has this fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Push even when the gist already matches the snippet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>

